Finding: ensureGroupFeeSummary()'s once-per-session latch (_groupFeesRequested)
is never reset. resetGroupFees() exists (checkout_controller.dart:1312-1316)
specifically to clear it "when the basket/address changes" per its own comment,
but is never called anywhere in the codebase (grep -rn "resetGroupFees()"
UserApp/lib/ returns only the definition, zero call sites).

Effect observed live (this QA session, emulator-5554, worktree backend
127.0.0.1:8050): a multi-store checkout's per-store fee/distance summary
(_perStoreDistanceKm via prepareGroupDeliveryData) is computed exactly ONCE,
using whatever delivery address was active at that FIRST multi-store checkout
visit in the app's process lifetime. Switching the delivery address afterwards
(via the checkout's own "Edit address" bottom sheet, notify:true) updates the
header/notice/ETA banor via the single-store getDistanceInKM path correctly,
but the group per-store fee breakdown silently keeps showing the STALE
first-computed values - it does not recompute for the new address.

Reproduction:
1. Multi-store cart (2+ stores), proceed to checkout with an in-zone address
   -> group fee summary computes once (clean).
2. Tap "Edit address" -> select a different (e.g. out-of-zone) saved address.
3. Observe: isOutOfZone banner + ETA banner + Place Order-disabled all update
   correctly (single-store code path), but the per-store fee breakdown does
   NOT recompute against the new address.

Scope note: NOT part of NEARS-2423's diff (ConfigController.php +
checkout_controller.dart lines 725/1207 only). This is pre-existing NEARS-1291
group-order-checkout code in the same file, discovered incidentally while
exercising the group-checkout path for NEARS-2423's item #3 ask. Recommend a
follow-up ticket to wire resetGroupFees() into the address-change call sites
(delivery_section.dart / address_bottom_sheet.dart onTap handlers).
